course: dictionary
lesson: 15934
title: Unresolved
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The prefix un- often means not, so unresolved means not yet resolved. Resolved means solved or settled, so unresolved means still open and not yet answered. «The argument between Sam and Priya is still unresolved.» The argument is not finished, and nobody has settled it yet.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The mystery ends with an unresolved question, so we never learn who took the key.» The clues say the mystery is not solved, so unresolved fits. Ask yourself: is this finished, or is it still open? If it is still open, unresolved is the word.
explain: Unresolved is often used for problems, arguments and questions. «Their unresolved fight made them avoid each other all week.» An unresolved problem keeps going until someone fixes it. To check, swap in "not yet solved" for unresolved. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Unresolved means not yet settled, solved or answered.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, as in «unhappy» and «unfair».
fact: «Unresolved issues» are problems that still need to be fixed.
fact: In science, an unresolved question is one that has no answer yet.
fact: Resolved is the opposite of unresolved: it means solved or settled.
exercise: «The mystery at the end of the book is still unresolved.» What does unresolved mean? | *Not yet solved | Very long | Bright and shiny | Finished and solved
exercise: What does the un- at the start of unresolved mean? | *Not | Very | Before | Again
exercise: «The scientists have an unresolved question about the new plant.» Is the question answered? | *No, it is still open | Yes, it was answered at once | Yes, the scientists are happy | Yes, it was a yes or no question
test: «The unresolved problem kept Maya awake at night.» What kept Maya awake? | Her new bike | *The unresolved problem | The sunny weather | A loud dog outside
test: «After the talk, the two friends finally resolved their argument.» What does resolved mean here? | *Settled | Started | Made bigger | Forgotten about
exam: What is the opposite of unresolved? | Broken | Unknown | Late | *Resolved
